{
	"description": "Golden vectors for the llm_prompt parameter of the llm_prompt_prediction action: which prompt profile a binding runs and how many predictions it asks for. Replayed by the macOS, Linux and Windows suites and by the action picker page.",
	"rule": "The value is \"<profile_id>\" (the AI menu's prediction count) or \"<profile_id>|<count>\" (a count of its own). The id is 1 to 128 letters, digits, _ or -. The count is a decimal integer from 1 to 10. Anything else, including spacing, is invalid. Whether the profile exists is checked when the action runs, not here. A vector without num_predictions expects none (the menu count); a vector with valid false expects a refusal. Only the translate profile may append |language; runtime admission validates the shared language byte bound and Unicode.",
